What does requiring this module yield?
```js
// thing.js
exports = { hello: false };
```

answer:
`import.meta`: modern Node has `import.meta.dirname` and `import.meta.filename` directly; older versions derive them from `import.meta.url`:
```js
import { fileURLToPath } from 'node:url';
import { dirname } from 'node:path';
const __filename = fileURLToPath(import.meta.url);
const __dirname = dirname(__filename);
```

